\import{discrete-macros}

\title{#{\ext{x}{D}P(x)}}
\date{2026-02-09T12:10:42Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\p{To prove a proposition of the form #{\ext{x}{D} P(x)}, give a specific example #{d} of an element in the domain #{D}, and prove #{P(d)}.}

\p{If you know #{\ext{x}{D} P(x)}, then you know #{P(d)}, where #{d} is a arbitrary element of the domain #{D} (with a newly made up variable name).}
